Cell["\<\
One possibility would be to use these two models separately. 

An additional possibility that would be easier, in some sense, would be to \
build on some existing models. In particular, a type III functional response \
can generate bistability under a particularly fluky situation - if the immune \
response can be treated as a constant, then a type III functional response on \
the parasite would generate bistability between a low parasite biomass and a \
high parasite biomass.
\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.796049927701849*^9, 3.796049935925342*^9}, {
  3.796056900229446*^9, 3.796056992546267*^9}, {3.796057394937532*^9, 
  3.796057429181758*^9}, {3.796062145714224*^9, 3.796062153734942*^9}, {
  3.796067439405542*^9, 3.7960675163693857`*^9}, {3.796071103167226*^9, 
  3.796071107983368*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"91dad7a2-7896-4647-98f6-\
04bf327b5e1d"],

