Cell["\<\
It\[CloseCurlyQuote]s much faster at higher cell densities. That\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s a key thing to note: polarization occurs more quickly as \
more T cells are recruited. Basically, the immune system makes decisions \
faster the more T cells there are in an area.  By the time you get to very \
high T cell populations, polarization can happen within a few days. That \
makes perfect sense, since the more cells there are, the more they are \
sending out signals to drive polarization. 

Note, however, that the equilibrium level of cytokine expression is not \
strongly affected by cell density - it goes up with cell density, but not a \
lot.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.796131906057621*^9, 3.796131984166831*^9}, {
  3.796132045737996*^9, 3.7961320680249557`*^9}, {3.7961324924777822`*^9, 
  3.796132580699586*^9}, {3.796132649022161*^9, 
  3.796132656097636*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0fb6025f-e016-422f-abfb-\
0991ab9ddc68"],

