Cell["\<\
You can see that transcription factor expression is, for the most part, \
insensitive to cell density. Total cytokine is, of course, much more closely \
related to cell density, and is a saturating function for the cytokine that \
is being expressed (in this case, CY2).  Thus, if we were going to make a \
simplified model, you would want cytokine expression to be a saturating \
function of cell density.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.796133935533867*^9, {3.796134111154636*^9, 3.796134150653391*^9}, {
   3.796134183109548*^9, 
   3.796134349520179*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ed9606c5-cd54-49c8-881a-\
e8606a399f5e"],

