Cell[TextData[{
 "Note that the lines th1=0 and th2=0 are ",
 StyleBox["not",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " isoclines for this system because of baseline Th cell-independent \
proliferation.  This is important because it means that only the \
intersections of the two lines above are possible equilibria of the system. \
In order to have multi-stability, the isoclines must cross at multiple \
places. This will be most easily facilitated by the slope of the isoclines \
changing signs.\n\nTaking the derivatives of the isoclines with respect to \
the Th cell populations, you can see that the baseline immune supply \
parameters ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", "i"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->"TraditionalForm",ExpressionUUID->
  "2a22d641-b309-4fad-b8f4-91978c9c8f99"],
 " are critical in determining the shape of the isocline. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.797249302377695*^9, 3.7972493705189943`*^9}, {
   3.797249454672964*^9, 3.797249573660658*^9}, {3.797249624737336*^9, 
   3.797249683719603*^9}, {3.797249718741274*^9, 3.7972498274161167`*^9}, 
   3.7972499895292997`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"8193c4a0-8a21-420d-811c-\
4bb00df08723"],

